# omnigent-ae server settings. Copy to config/server.env (gitignored; no secrets
# in it). deploy/compose.sh hands this file to compose twice: for interpolating
# the compose files (the image, the host port, the data directory) and as the
# omnigent service's env_file.
#
# Secrets are NOT here: compose.sh loads them after this file, from
# config/secrets.env whenever that file exists (it says so on every run), else
# from /secure/env/omnigent-ae.env (deploy/pull-secrets.sh). A try-out needs one:
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD. The full list is commented at the end of this file.
#
# The REQUIRED block is enough for a server on this machine with username and
# password sign-in (README.md, "Quick start"). Everything after it is optional.
# Variable names were checked against the pinned upstream (upstream.lock):
# deploy/docker/docker-compose.yaml, omnigent/server/ws_origin.py,
# server_config.py, accounts_secret.py, routes/device_auth.py, and
# packages/ae_omni_policies/README.md.

# ════ REQUIRED ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# The image: ghcr.io/<owner>/<repo>, the package a repository's AE_IMAGE
# variable gives .github/workflows/image.yml. The public build is below.
AE_IMAGE=ghcr.io/analyticendeavors/omnigent-ae-public
# The tag to run, ae-vX.Y.Z.N: the newest one on the Releases page. There is no
# `latest`. deploy/auto-update.sh rewrites this line when a newer tag is
# published (deploy/README.md, "Automatic updates").
OMNIGENT_IMAGE_TAG=ae-vX.Y.Z.N
# Host port on 127.0.0.1 (the container keeps 8000); any free port. Change
# OMNIGENT_ACCOUNTS_BASE_URL and OMNIGENT_WS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS below with it.
OMNIGENT_PORT=8010
# Where the database and the server's files live on this machine, an absolute
# path: <dir>/postgres and <dir>/data, created by Docker on first start (owned
# by root and by Postgres's uid 70, so removing them needs sudo). Unset means
# /secure/omnigent, the encrypted volume of the full deploy (deploy/README.md,
# step 2). For a try-out: the full deploy's nightly dump and backup paths stay
# under /secure and do not follow this setting.
# AE_DATA_DIR=/srv/omnigent-ae

# Sign-in. With OMNIGENT_AUTH_ENABLED=1 and no OIDC issuer, the server uses its
# own accounts: the first visit shows "Create the admin account", the cookie
# secret is minted into the data directory on first start, and `omnigent login
# <base URL>` on a host asks for that username and password. Microsoft (or any
# OIDC) sign-in instead: the optional block below.
OMNIGENT_AUTH_ENABLED=1
# The URL browsers and hosts use, exactly (hosts store their login keyed by it,
# and config/host.env's OMNIGENT_SERVER_URL must match it character for
# character). On a tailnet: https://<box-hostname>.<tailnet>.ts.net:8010
# (deploy/README.md, step 7).
OMNIGENT_ACCOUNTS_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8010
# Origins allowed for WebSocket upgrades and uploads, comma separated: the base
# URL, plus any other name in front of the server (a phone off the tailnet gets
# WebSocket close 4403 and HTTP 403 without its origin here). Exact origins:
# scheme and host, no path, no trailing slash, the port only when the URL
# carries one. With a public hostname too:
# OMNIGENT_WS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://<box-hostname>.<tailnet>.ts.net:8010,https://omnigent.<your-domain>
OMNIGENT_WS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://127.0.0.1:8010

# ════ OPTIONAL ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Postgres identity inside the stack; the defaults match upstream's compose.
# POSTGRES_USER=omnigent
# POSTGRES_DB=omnigent

# ── OIDC sign-in (Microsoft Entra ID shown) ────────────────────────────────
# Replaces the accounts above; the accounts-to-OIDC remap and the app
# registration are in deploy/README.md, "Adding an OIDC provider". The two
# secrets (OMNIGENT_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET, OMNIGENT_OIDC_COOKIE_SECRET) go in the
# secrets file.
# OMNIGENT_AUTH_PROVIDER=oidc
# OMNIGENT_OIDC_ISSUER=https://login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant-id>/v2.0
# The app's Application (client) ID. Not a secret.
# OMNIGENT_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=<entra-app-client-id>
# One callback host only: upstream fixes the redirect at startup and the state
# and session cookies are __Host- (host-only), so only this origin can sign in;
# list it in OMNIGENT_WS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS too. A CLI or host login opens
# /auth/login?ticket=... on its own server URL: open the same path on this host
# instead (the ticket lives in the server process, so the CLI's poll on the
# other URL still completes).
# OMNIGENT_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=https://omnigent.<your-domain>/auth/callback
# Entra v2 ID tokens carry no email_verified, so the identity comes from
# preferred_username (the UPN) and the verification check is skipped; safe
# when the tenant and an app assignment already restrict who signs in. A UPN
# can be renamed; the next login is then a new user until the remap in
# deploy/README.md, "Adding an OIDC provider", moves the data across.
# OMNIGENT_OIDC_EMAIL_CLAIM=preferred_username
# OMNIGENT_OIDC_SKIP_EMAIL_VERIFICATION=1
# OMNIGENT_OIDC_ALLOWED_DOMAINS=<your-domain>
# Hours a sign-in lasts; 720 is 30 days.
# OMNIGENT_OIDC_SESSION_TTL_HOURS=720

# Days a host or CLI that ran `omnigent login` may keep refreshing before a
# person logs in again, counted from the login's approval and checked on every
# refresh; upstream's default is 30 (routes/device_auth.py). 90 here, so an
# unattended host survives a long absence: when it lapses, the host stops with
# exit status 78 and stays stopped, taking its sessions and scheduled agents
# with it, until someone runs `omnigent login` again. Read once at server start
# (deploy/README.md, "Re-login").
OMNIGENT_GRANT_MAX_LIFETIME_DAYS=90
# The accounts cookie secret: minted on first start when unset (above). Set it
# only to share one secret across several server instances.
# OMNIGENT_ACCOUNTS_COOKIE_SECRET=

# ── The server's files inside the container ────────────────────────────────
# Both from the image itself since 2026-09-24, so a release carries its own
# config and agents and deploying a tag needs no copy step (the auto-update
# timer in deploy/README.md cannot write /secure/omnigent, which is 700 root).
# Before that the box pointed these at hand-made copies under /data
# (/secure/omnigent/data); those copies are now unused. The price: a spec or
# config change on the box is a commit and a tag, not an edit in place.
OMNIGENT_CONFIG=/opt/ae/config/server.yaml
# The two scheduled agents and the orchestrator (2026-09-25). Append
# :/opt/ae/agents/reviewer-codex to turn the reviewer on. A box whose line still
# names only steward and shutdown gets the orchestrator anyway: the image's
# entrypoint appends it (ae_omni_policies/docker_entrypoint.py);
# AE_EXTRA_AGENTS=off stops that.
OMNIGENT_BUILTIN_AGENT_DIRS=/opt/ae/agents/steward:/opt/ae/agents/shutdown:/opt/ae/agents/orchestrator
# Release features: upstream's comma-separated OMNIGENT_FEATURES. The image's
# entrypoint appends sidebar_grouping_ui (2026-10-19), which the sidebar's
# Triage grouping and Manual order build on, whenever the installed omnigent
# still knows the name (an unknown name stops the server at startup);
# AE_EXTRA_FEATURES=off stops that.
# OMNIGENT_FEATURES=harness_install

# ── The AE layer (packages/ae_omni_policies/README.md) ─────────────────────
# task-store's origin; the Cloudflare Access service token for it is in the
# secrets file. Unset, the Parking Lot and its tools are off (there is no
# default origin).
# AE_TASK_STORE_URL=https://tasks.<your-domain>
# IANA zone for resurface dates, the lot's "today", and the clock the seeded
# steward, shutdown and check-in schedules run on; unset, UTC (2026-10-22).
# AE_TASK_STORE_TZ=Europe/London
# Key Vault expiry alerts (2026-10-23): a task with a phone alarm when a secret's
# expiry is 30 and 7 days away and when it passes. The list they land in, by name
# (unset: no list), the alarm time on the clock above, and the off switch.
# AE_SECRET_ALERT_LIST=Work
# AE_SECRET_ALERT_TIME=09:00
# AE_SECRET_ALERTS=off
# Slots: working sessions allowed at once, the one setting for the slot cap and every count in the UI (2026-09-24); change it, then `deploy/compose.sh up -d --force-recreate omnigent`.
AE_SLOT_LIMIT=3
# New scheduled tasks file their run sessions into this sidebar project, by name,
# when the create names none (2026-10-13, patch 0033). A task's
# own project, set in the automation dialog, wins. Unset: runs stay unfiled.
# OMNIGENT_SCHEDULED_TASK_DEFAULT_PROJECT=Automation Notes
# Auto-resume (2026-10-13, patch 0034): when a host reconnects after a restart, its
# sessions that were mid-turn relaunch and continue by themselves, one try per dead
# runner, if touched within six hours. On unless set to 0.
# AE_AUTO_RESUME=1
# Merge watcher (2026-10-21, packages/ae_omni_policies/src/ae_omni_policies/merge_watch.py):
# every 10 s it asks GitHub (AE_GITHUB_TOKEN, conditional reads) about the open pull
# requests attached to sessions, and posts one note into the session when one merges or
# closes, so the session continues by itself. State lives in /data/ae-merge-watch.json
# (AE_MERGE_WATCH_FILE overrides). On unless set to 0; off without a GitHub token.
# AE_MERGE_WATCH=1
# Auto-archive (2026-10-24, packages/ae_omni_policies/src/ae_omni_policies/auto_archive.py):
# Reid closes a finished chat by setting it to reference, and it then sat in his list.
# Every 60 s the server archives each idle top-level session that has been in reference
# for AE_AUTO_ARCHIVE_MINUTES (default 10), through the same PATCH the web uses. The
# clocks live in /data/ae-auto-archive.json (AE_AUTO_ARCHIVE_FILE overrides; set it empty
# for memory only). A chat that got a follow-up turn waits again, a session shared with
# anyone besides its owner is never archived, and one the sweep archived and you then
# unarchived stays until its status leaves reference and returns. On unless 0.
# AE_AUTO_ARCHIVE=1
# AE_AUTO_ARCHIVE_MINUTES=10
# The gate reply posts through a real HTTP loopback to the server itself;
# inside the container that is port 8000, whatever the host publishes.
AE_SELF_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
# The Graphiti MCP the steward and shutdown agents read as box_memory
# (2026-10-21). The image's entrypoint writes it into both specs before they
# register (ae_omni_policies/docker_entrypoint.py); unset, they register without
# that server and the container log says so. Set it to your Graphiti MCP's URL
# or leave it commented.
# AE_GRAPH_MCP_URL=http://<graphiti-host>:8000/mcp
# Resume on the Parking Lot page starts a Claude Code session on the one online
# host, in its home directory (2026-09-24). Set these only to change that: a
# host name or id when more than one host is online, an absolute workspace, or
# another built-in agent.
# AE_RESUME_HOST=<box-hostname>
# AE_RESUME_WORKSPACE=<your-home-dir>
# AE_RESUME_AGENT=claude-native-ui
# Where the newest plan-limits snapshot per harness is kept, so a restart shows
# the last reading instead of nothing until the host relay's next five-minute
# tick (docs/PLAN-LIMITS.md, 2026-09-24). Unset: /data/ae-limits.json when
# /data exists, else memory only (2026-10-20; the box's live env had lost the
# line, and every deploy blanked the Usage card for one relay tick).
# AE_LIMITS_STATE_FILE=/data/ae-limits.json
# Where each user's manual sidebar order is kept, so it follows them from one
# device to the next (2026-10-19). Unset: /data/ae-sidebar.json when /data
# exists, else memory only.
# AE_SIDEBAR_STATE_FILE=/data/ae-sidebar.json
# Where each user's role presets are kept (Settings > Roles, GET and PUT
# /v1/ae/roles, 2026-10-23); the lead's notice reads them every turn. Unset:
# /data/ae-roles.json when /data exists, else memory only.
# AE_ROLES_STATE_FILE=/data/ae-roles.json
# Where the deploy hold is kept (the Admin Center's Deploys section,
# 2026-10-19): deploy/auto-update.sh reads it through compose.sh exec, so it
# must be a path inside the container. Unset: /data/ae-deploy-hold.json when
# /data exists, else memory only (and the script never sees a hold).
# AE_DEPLOY_HOLD_FILE=/data/ae-deploy-hold.json
# Where the box host's reconnect state is kept (the Admin Center's Box host
# section, 2026-10-20): the folder holding ae-host-relink-status.json and
# ae-host-relink-request.json, which deploy/host-relink.sh reads and writes
# through compose.sh exec, so it must be a path inside the container. Unset:
# /data when it exists, else memory only (and the helper never sees a request).
# AE_HOST_RELINK_DIR=/data
# The Your move page (2026-09-24): which repos its pull request section reads,
# whose pull requests count, and whose sessions are the steward's brief. (The
# PR cards and Open PRs read whatever repos the sessions track, not this list.)
# Without AE_GITHUB_REPOS the section asks for it; without AE_GITHUB_LOGIN it
# counts the token's own login. The token itself is a secret (end of this file).
# AE_GITHUB_REPOS=<your-org>/<your-repo>
# The repo the Deploys section reads release tags from (release.py); the
# default is analyticendeavors/omnigent-ae-public. Set it when you publish your own fork's image.
# AE_RELEASE_REPO=<your-org>/<your-fork>
# AE_GITHUB_LOGIN=<your-github-login>
# AE_STEWARD_AGENT=steward
# The Admin Center's Databricks section (2026-10-19): the workspace whose SQL
# warehouses it lists and whose system.billing tables feed the spend strip.
# The section stays off until the two secrets below are also present. The
# credit settings are the defaults; CADENCE picks which bar leads (monthly: this
# month's spend, once: spend since CREDIT_START), and both bars always show.
# AE_DATABRICKS_HOST=https://<your-workspace>.cloud.databricks.com
# The Admin Center's Azure card (azure_cost.py): the subscriptions to read, <guid>=<name>, comma separated.
# Its service principal comes from Key Vault through deploy/pull-secrets.sh.
# AE_AZURE_COST_SUBSCRIPTIONS=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000=Production
# Where the card's last reading is kept, so a restart shows it at once instead
# of "Reading..." (2026-10-22). Unset: /data/ae-azure-cost.json; empty: memory only.
# AE_AZURE_COST_STATE_FILE=/data/ae-azure-cost.json
# Cost targets on the Azure card (2026-10-25, cost_targets.py): a limit on spend or on a
# running Fabric capacity, and a task with a phone alarm when it is crossed. Where the
# targets are kept (unset: /data/ae-cost-targets.json; empty: memory only), where the
# filed alerts are kept (unset: /data/ae-cost-alerts.json; empty: memory only), and the
# task-store list the alerts land in, by name (unset: AE Work).
# AE_COST_TARGETS_FILE=/data/ae-cost-targets.json
# AE_COST_ALERT_STATE_FILE=/data/ae-cost-alerts.json
# AE_COST_ALERT_LIST=AE Work
# AE_DATABRICKS_CREDIT_USD=200
# AE_DATABRICKS_CREDIT_CADENCE=once
# AE_DATABRICKS_CREDIT_START=<yyyy-mm-dd>
# AE_DATABRICKS_CREDIT_END=<yyyy-mm-dd>
# AE_DATABRICKS_STATE_FILE=/data/ae-databricks.json
# The Admin Center's Fabric capacity prices (2026-10-21): the F SKU pay-as-you-go
# price per capacity unit per hour, in US dollars. F2 is 2 units, so F4 at the
# default is $0.72/h. Each row's $/h and the resize confirm use it. The capacity
# list itself needs the two secrets AE_FABRIC_CAPACITIES_URL and
# AE_FABRIC_CAPACITIES_KEY (Key Vault fabric-capacities-url and
# fabric-capacities-key; end of this file).
# AE_FABRIC_USD_PER_CU_HOUR=0.18

# ── Optional: the policy model for the fork-suspect classifier ─────────────
# Off unless config/server.yaml's llm: block is uncommented. The Ollama example
# there reaches the box through host.docker.internal (the compose override adds
# the host-gateway entry) and needs no key. The Anthropic example reads:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=            (a secret: put it in /secure/env/omnigent-ae.env)

# ── Secrets: written by deploy/pull-secrets.sh to /secure/env/omnigent-ae.env ─
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=            Key Vault omnigent-ae-postgres-password
# AE_CF_ACCESS_CLIENT_ID=       Key Vault cf-access-svc-taskstore-client-id
# AE_CF_ACCESS_CLIENT_SECRET=   Key Vault cf-access-svc-taskstore-client-secret
# OMNIGENT_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=  Key Vault omnigent-oidc-client-secret (the Entra app's)
# OMNIGENT_OIDC_COOKIE_SECRET=  Key Vault omnigent-oidc-cookie-secret (64 hex chars)
# AE_GITHUB_TOKEN=              Key Vault omnigent-ae-github-token (optional; Contents and
#                               Pull requests read and write, Checks and Commit statuses
#                               read, Workflows read and write, since the PR cards' Merge
#                               button, 2026-09-24; without it the Dashboard's pull
#                               request sections say how to add it)
# AE_GIT_SWEEP_CONFIG=          optional, the Admin Center's Git repos card (2026-10-24): owner/repo:path
#                               of a Dependency Sweep config JSON (its repos and catchUpBranches)
# AE_GIT_REPOS=                 optional, comma-separated owner/repo added to that list
# AE_GIT_VIEW_ONLY=             optional, comma-separated owner/repo shown but left out of the totals
# AE_GIT_SWEEP_WORKFLOW=        optional, the sweep workflow file (default dependency-sweep.yml)
# AE_GIT_KEEP_BRANCHES=         optional, comma-separated owner/repo:branch kept on purpose; listed
#                               on the Git repos card but not counted as old branches
# AE_GIT_TOKEN_<OWNER>=         optional secret, one read-only token per owner (owner upper-cased,
#                               non-alphanumerics as _); falls back to AE_GITHUB_TOKEN
# AE_FABRIC_WAKE_URL_<NAME>=         optional, one per Fabric capacity: its wake Logic
#                                    App's URL (2026-10-16); the capacity is <name>
#                                    lower-cased; the Secrets card lists each one set
# AE_FABRIC_SUSPEND_KEY_<NAME>=      optional; turns on Off for that capacity; without
#                                    it the card has Wake only
# AE_FABRIC_CAPACITIES_URL=          Key Vault fabric-capacities-url (optional, with the next
#                                    one; the shared la-fabric-capacities Logic App, 2026-10-21:
#                                    every Fabric capacity on the Compute card, with Pause,
#                                    Start and resize; see AE_FABRIC_USD_PER_CU_HOUR above)
# AE_FABRIC_CAPACITIES_KEY=          Key Vault fabric-capacities-key (optional; 64 hex chars,
#                                    sent as the x-capacity-key header)
# AE_DATABRICKS_CLIENT_ID=       Key Vault databricks-mvp-client-id (optional; the Admin
#                                Center's Databricks section, 2026-10-19, with the next one)
# AE_DATABRICKS_CLIENT_SECRET=   Key Vault databricks-mvp-client-secret (optional; the
#                                ae-admin-center service principal's OAuth secret, scope sql)
# AE_SHARED_ACCOUNTS_KEY=        Key Vault omnigent-ae-shared-accounts-key (optional; the
#                                Fernet key that encrypts shared Claude accounts' tokens,
#                                2026-10-20; without it none can be added or used.
#                                deploy/README.md, "Shared Claude accounts")
